ration work touches both TrustyAI\n96\t  and the Llama Stack distribution surface. Per the single-most-relevant-\n97\t  component rule it is assigned canonical component `TrustyAI` (the guardrails\n98\t  are \"via TrustyAI\"); cross-team coordination with RHOAI GenAI is recorded as\n99\t  a risk on the epic. If Llama Stack-distribution-side wiring turns out to be\n100\t  substantial code work, split it into a RHOAI GenAI-owned implementation epic\n101\t  blocked by this one (Rule 12).\n102\t- **Architecture claims corroborated:** all three components have architecture\n103\t  context files (`rhoai-3.0/llama-stack.md`, `trustyai.md`, `dashboard.md`)\n104\t  corroborating the strategy's Tech Preview premise for Llama Stack — no\n105\t  contradictions found. Llama Stack is Konflux-onboarded and midstream-hosted,\n106\t  so no onboarding chain epics are needed.\n107\t\n108\t## Tiered Delivery\n109\t\n110\tNot applicable in the Rule 16-18 sense — there is no external dependency with\n111\tuncertain timing (no upstream PR/RFC or vendor gating). The internal gating\n112\tunknown (E001) blocks only E002/E003; E004 (TrustyAI integration) and E005\n113\t(Dashboard default enablement) deliver independent partial value and run in\n114\tparallel from the start, which is the practical Tier 1 / gated split for this\n115\tstrategy.\n116\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8385305d62eab0a5","agent_id":"aadbfefa472cec417","session_id":"45850d2e-0f91-4d60-8339-ec068a16e17f","uuid":"78b10e41-e45f-4cdf-85eb-b459221ea7fb","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:24:17.903Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b128c7114e9f1c92","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
