on per gap (fix-for-GA, accept, defer) and the hardening work required to close the fix-for-GA items\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- A GA-readiness report exists that enumerates gaps in each of the four dimensions (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), each with a severity and a disposition\n49\t- The gap inventory is grounded in consolidated TP support-ticket feedback and repository/API evidence, not anecdote\n50\t- The definitive GA scope is recorded and accepted by strategy stakeholders as the planning baseline for the graduation work\n51\t- Downstream hardening work (API stability guarantees, production support posture) can be scoped directly from the report without further discovery\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- HLR-1 (P0): GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between current TP quality and GA bar, producing the definitive GA scope\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a239b36a113a9dd1","agent_id":"a3ecef42eb32128d9","session_id":"45850d2e-0f91-4d60-8339-ec068a16e17f","uuid":"5071011f-b358-4eae-aa02-ecb727003673","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:30:44.735Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8f9b5e98e959c29","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
