eleases\n52\t- Integration of the supported TrustyAI guardrails integration documentation into the GA documentation set: the TrustyAI supported-integration work authors the content (configuration, capabilities, limitations); this epic uplifts it to GA documentation standards, links it from the Llama Stack documentation, and strips any remaining experimental-flag framing\n53\t- Integration of the production support posture — SLO targets, backport policy, and the supported configuration matrix, published as the authoritative artifacts by the support-posture work — into the GA documentation set: surfaced, cross-linked, and presented consistently, not re-authored\n54\t- Updated guidance for default Dashboard enablement on entitled clusters, replacing TP opt-in instructions\n55\t- Removal or revision of TP-era caveats and experimental-flag instructions\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- The documentation set meets GA standards for accuracy and completeness\n60\t- Migration notes cover moving from TP releases (including the last two) to the GA release\n61\t- All content is technically reviewed against the implemented GA behavior by the owning engineers\n62\t- Each externally-owned deliverable — the TrustyAI guardrails integration documentation and the three support-posture artifacts (SLO targets, backport policy, supported configuration matrix) — appears in the GA documentation set exactly once, sourced from its owning deliverable with no duplicated or divergent re-authoring\n63\t- No TP-era experimental-flag or opt-in instructions remain in the GA documentation set\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-6 (P2): Documentation uplifted to GA standards, including migration notes from TP\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a239b36a113a9dd1","agent_id":"a3ecef42eb32128d9","session_id":"45850d2e-0f91-4d60-8339-ec068a16e17f","uuid":"d47a98bb-4ee7-4bf1-a0c9-053bceba7905","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:30:51.131Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-too