 Rule-mandated\nACs are all present: E002 (a replacement epic for TP-era API behavior) carries\na detailed rollback/compatibility safeguard AC requiring an executed test with\nrecorded evidence; E005 carries a feature-flag rollback AC verified as a\nworking path; E006 (docs-authoring) carries the technical-review-by-owning-\nengineers AC; no konflux-chain epics exist, so no build-pipeline AC is\nrequired. No soft-ACs found: E001's \"accepted by strategy stakeholders\" AC\nconditions the epic's own deliverable (ratification of the report it produces),\nnot an externally-granted availability, and E005's entitlement ACs condition\nwhat the epic itself verifies. No epic body references sibling epics by draft\nID — cross-epic references use descriptive names (\"the GA-readiness\nassessment\", \"the support-posture work\"), which survive Jira submission.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n\nAll strategy scope is accounted for: the problem statement's four gap\ndimensions (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling) are\ninventoried by E001 and dispositioned downstream (fix-for-GA gaps closed by\nE002; scale-limit/error-handling findings folded into E003's config matrix);\nthe scattered TP feedback is consolidated by E001's scope; every HLR maps to an\nepic; all three affected components (Llama Stack, TrustyAI, Dashboard) have\nowning epics. Out-of-scope constraints are respected — E004 explicitly scopes\nto GA-bar quality/support work, excluding new guardrails feature development,\nand nothing deprecates alternative serving paths. Strategy-level context is\ncarried forward, not dropped: Open Question 1 becomes E001 plus the gating\nmetadata on E002/E003 plus the sizing Health Warning; missing strategy sections\n(no Impacted Teams table, no dependencies table, no NFRs) are recorded as\nnon-blocking Health Warnings with the assumptions made explicit (owner teams\ntaken from architecture context; docs team assumption named). Documentation\nsupport is required by HLR-6 and the docs-authoring epic E006 exists, blocked\nby all implementations per Rule 11. No conditional branches are stated by the\nstrategy, so none are needed. Tiered delivery is correctly assessed as\nnot-applicable (no external dependency with uncertain timing) with the\npractical parallel partial value (E004/E005) identified.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26998,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a239b36a113a9dd1","agent_id":"a3ecef42eb32128d9","session_id":"45850d2e-0f91-4d60-8339-ec068a16e17f","uuid":"2839f229-532c-440f-b478-0cd5f5cac396","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:32:48.231Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
